-`impl-test` adds a test only with a gap proof: a seeded defect its unit's existing tests miss, or a search finding no test of the unit; otherwise the decision is `none`. A new case for a contract an existing test owns extends that test. A fixed behaviour defect keeps the regression duty only when running code reproduces it, proven fail-first; a prose or rule fix adds a test only for a token a machine parses. A one-time sweep test is named `temporary(<NNN>)` and the next sprint's `impl-test` removes it. `test-delta` flags a sprint adding more test lines than other code and asks for an `Allowance`. A sprint can instead ask for a suite revision: the tester dedupes, speeds up and splits the suite area by area, each surviving test proven against a seeded defect.
+`impl-test` adds a test only with a gap proof: a seeded defect its unit's existing tests miss, or a search finding no test of the unit; otherwise the decision is `none`. A new case for a contract an existing test owns extends that test. A fixed behaviour defect keeps the regression duty only when running code reproduces it, proven fail-first; a prose or rule fix adds a test only for a token a machine parses. A one-time sweep test is named `temporary(<NNN>)` and the next sprint's `impl-test` removes it. `test-delta` flags a sprint adding more test lines than other code and asks for an `Allowance`. Escape literal pipes in test-plan table cells, including inside code spans. A migration adding a required column backfills live and rotated plans or explicitly exempts earlier rows. A sprint can instead ask for a suite revision: the tester dedupes, speeds up and splits the suite area by area, each surviving test proven against a seeded defect.
 
 **Where do TODO stubs live?**
 Project-globally in `.asd/project/stubs.md`; it holds only open stubs, and a stub is deleted on resolution. The registry persists across sprint archival. The PR phase blocks if any stub introduced by the current sprint remains unresolved without an `(accepted-debt)` Reason prefix.
